Support files for launching haiku from /etc/rc.d/ on FreeBSD

To install haiku on FreeBSD, run the following commands as root inside this directory:

```
# (Optional) Install build dependencies
pkg install -y gmake rsync

# Build haiku
pushd ../..
./configure
gmake -j
gmake install
popd

# Install haiku as rc.d service. Make sure you are in the containing directory of this README file.
rsync -r tree/ /
mkdir -p /etc/haiku.d/boot.d

# enable haiku (to start on next boot)
/etc/rc.d/haiku enable
# start haiku now
/etc/rc.d/haiku start
```
